HST Office: every large ribbon button shows a 24 px image (owner rule; Paste alone stays larger).

Large buttons of the four Tabbed ribbons that named a 32 px (cmd/32/) or 16 px (cmd/sc_) image now name the
24 px one (cmd/lc_), and the 32 px toolboxes of the Extensions tabs (icon_size 5) become 24 px (3), like every
other large button: Writer's Page Border, Insert Citation, Citation Library, Accessibility Check, Where Is the
Command, Report an Error and the Extensions tab; Sheets', Slides' and Draw's Extensions tabs; Slides' transition
and animation previews; Draw's Open in HST PDF. Two images have no HST glyph at any size and take the nearest one
that every icon style draws: Where Is the Command shows helpindex (was extendedhelp), the previews show
presentationcurrentslide (was runbasic). Every other image is drawn at 24 px by the HST styles, the classic style
(Colibre, or the HST layer where Colibre lacks it) and the modern styles.

License: these upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0).
